+V64.3.25 EAF-ICER-DRC engineering validation
+================================================
+
+Scope
+-----
+Delivery derived from uploaded V64.3.24 code.  Current uploaded V64.3.24 result is a legitimate pre-fresh TRAIN STOP; V25 carries only the pre-registered surviving aggregate-downside branch to fresh validation.
+
+Engineering/protocol fixes in this delivery
+-------------------------------------------
+1. V25 TRAIN fitter streams only fields needed by the 18-D aggregate DRC representation instead of retaining the full 747MB JSON payload in memory.
+2. V25 fitter hard-checks exactly 3000 TRAIN scene identities.
+3. V25 fitter writes TRAIN cross-fit report and TRAIN token manifest before a fail-closed gate exit.
+4. V25 launcher preserves train_drc_fit stage timing and retained audit path on non-zero fitter exit.
+5. V25 launcher reuses V24 TRAIN frontier if available; explicit V24_TRAIN_EDGES override is supported; frozen replay is fallback only.
+6. V25 config metadata accurately distinguishes evidence-local mean-SE vs evidence-local downside certificate.
+7. V25 contract verifies 18-D schema, equal aggregate metric, fixed K32/K64, multiplier=1, certificate kind, memory SHA, scalar-only dominance, incumbent-default retention, replacement-only risk, structural delegation, and frozen V20 heads.
+8. Historical V24 fitter is diagnostic-only patched so a gate failure persists fit report/token manifest; its numerical gate and runtime action semantics are unchanged.
+9. Historical V24 aggregate model_type metadata is corrected from attribution-resolved naming to evidence-local naming; runtime dispatch was already evidence_only, so historical actions are unchanged.
+10. V25 fresh checker serializes selected direct-replacement tails in endpoint-regret and frontier teacher-improvement units.
